   "how": {
    "tpl": "Running watts: {{out.running_w|int}} W. Starting watts (running watts plus the largest start jump): {{out.peak_w|int}} W. Running watts × {{out.margin|2}} margin is compared with the starting watts; the larger, {{out.sized_w|int}} W, is what a generator must deliver (an inverter is checked on two ratings instead: its continuous rating against the running watts × margin, its surge rating against the starting watts). {{out.sized_w|int}} W ÷ {{out.pf|2}} ÷ 1,000 = {{out.recommended_kva|2}} kVA, so a {{out.standard_kva|1}} kVA generator.",
    "text": "Running watts: 200 W. Starting watts (running watts plus the largest start jump): 1,200 W. Running watts × 1.25 margin is compared with the starting watts; the larger, 1,200 W, is what a generator must deliver (an inverter is checked on two ratings instead: its continuous rating against the running watts × margin, its surge rating against the starting watts). 1,200 W ÷ 0.8 ÷ 1,000 = 1.5 kVA, so a 2.5 kVA generator."
   },
